  "program": {
    "source": "const A=4,C=1,K=0.4,R=0.14,N=64,S=2,LIM=8,MAXS=40,AS=2,X0=0.7,Z0=1.6;\nconst loss=(x,z)=>0.5*(A*x*x+C*z*z);\nconst rand=n=>{const v=Math.sin(n*12.9898+41.17)*43758.5453;return v-Math.floor(v);};\nconst gauss=n=>Math.sqrt(-2*Math.log(Math.max(1e-9,rand(n))))*Math.cos(2*Math.PI*rand(n+0.37));\nconst sd=b=>S*Math.sqrt(Math.max(0,N-b)/((N-1)*b));\nfunction next(s,inp){const b=Math.max(1,Math.round(Number(inp.batchSize))),lr=inp.learningRate,k=s.run*997+s.step*3+1,d=sd(b);return[-lr*(A*s.x+d*gauss(k)),-lr*(C*s.z+d*gauss(k+1.5))];}\nconst div=s=>loss(s.x,s.z)>LIM||Math.abs(s.x)>2||Math.abs(s.z)>2;\nconst word=s=>div(s)?'diverged':s.step>=MAXS?'finished':'running';\nconst over=s=>word(s)!=='running';\nfunction advance(s,inp){const[dx,dz]=next(s,inp),x=s.x+dx,z=s.z+dz;return{...s,x,z,step:s.step+1,path:s.path.concat([[x,z]])};}\nconst fresh=(run,kept)=>({x:X0,z:Z0,step:0,run,path:[[X0,Z0]],kept});\nexport function initialState(){return fresh(0,[]);}\nexport function reduce({state:s,event:e,inputs}){\n if(e.type==='step')return over(s)||e.tick%6?s:advance(s,inputs);\n if(e.type==='action'&&e.action==='newRun')return fresh(s.run+1,s.step>0?s.path:s.kept);\n return s;\n}\nconst lift=p=>[p[0],Math.min(K*loss(p[0],p[1]),4)+0.05,p[1]];\nfunction aim(dx,dz,on){const l=Math.hypot(dx,dz),h=Math.SQRT1_2;return on&&l>1e-6?{visible:true,quaternion:[dz/l*h,0,-dx/l*h,h],scale:[1,l*AS,1]}:{visible:false};}\nexport function evaluate({inputs,state}){\n const s=state||initialState(),L=loss(s.x,s.z),live=!over(s),[dx,dz]=next(s,inputs),lr=inputs.learningRate;\n return{nodes:{ball:{position:[s.x,K*Math.min(L,10)+R,s.z]},stepArrow:aim(dx,dz,live),trueArrow:aim(-lr*A*s.x,-lr*C*s.z,live&&inputs.showTrueGradient),trail:{points:s.path.map(lift)},ghost:{points:s.kept.map(lift)}},\n readouts:{status:word(s),loss:L,steps:s.step,stepLen:live?Math.hypot(dx,dz):0}};\n}\n"
  },
  "assumptions": [
    "Illustration: a made-up two-setting loss bowl with simulated batch noise, not a real model trained on real data.",
    "Loss = (4x² + z²)/2, drawn at height 0.4 × loss over x, z from −2 to 2. It is 4 times as steep in x, so overshooting starts there. Above a learning rate of 0.5, the x swings grow until the run diverges.",
    "Each step adds −learning rate × (true slope + noise). The noise is Gaussian with SD 2·√((64−b)/(63·b)) per direction for batch size b. It is largest at b = 1 and exactly zero at b = 64 (the whole data set).",
    "The orange arrow is the actual next step (against the noisy slope). The grey arrow is −learning rate × the true slope. Both are drawn at 2× the step length on the bowl, the same scale for both.",
    "A run takes up to 40 steps, one every 6 host ticks. It is marked diverged when the loss passes 8 or the ball leaves the drawn bowl. The Loss readout keeps the true value; the drawn height is capped.",
    "Noise comes from a fixed seed. Reset replays the same sequence. 'New run, keep last path' uses the next noise values and keeps the finished path as the faded ghost (max 41 points, start included).",
    "With noise, a step lowers the loss only on average. With small batches, single steps can raise it."
  ]
}